  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that CID 53630653 may be a target of multiple compounds that interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Specifically, the compound N-[(4R,10R,13S)-17-[1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-4-hydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl]-N,3-dimethylbut-2-enamide, and Broussoaurone A, both of which are targets of CID 53630653, are known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This indicates that CID 53630653 may be a potential modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, possibly through a mechanism involving the inhibition or regulation of its target proteins. The evidence is consistent with a role in the regulation of gene expression, as the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2), which is involved in epigenetic regulation. The scores from the different paths suggest that CID 53630653 is a relevant target in this context, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
